      "title": "About WPCNA",
      "url": "/about/",
      "type": "wpcna",
      "excerpt": "Learn what WPCNA is, how it supports White Plains neighborhood associations, and how residents can contact the council.",
      "text": "Learn what WPCNA is, how it supports White Plains neighborhood associations, and how residents can contact the council.\n\nAbout\n\nOur mission\n\n“The White Plains Council of Neighborhood Associations coordinates the neighborhood associations in White Plains, NY. Its purpose is to enhance the quality of life in the City, and in particular, in its neighborhoods. As an advisory council, the WPCNA functions by disseminating information and opinion to the public and public officials, and by encouraging local action.”\n\nArchived WPCNA mission statement\n\nWhat WPCNA does\n\nWPCNA is a forum for neighborhood associations across White Plains. Its role is practical: keep information moving, help associations stay connected, and support local action when neighborhood concerns need attention.\n\nShare information\n\nWPCNA helps circulate neighborhood concerns, meeting information, civic updates, and public-interest items that residents may otherwise have to find across several different sources.\n\nConnect associations\n\nThe council gives neighborhood associations a place to exchange ideas, compare concerns, and learn from one another.\n\nEncourage local action\n\nWhen issues affect neighborhoods, WPCNA helps residents stay organized, informed, and connected to the right public process.\n\nHow this site helps residents\n\nThis site brings together the most useful WPCNA and community information in one place.\n\nThe goal is simple: make it easier for residents to see what is happening, understand where it fits, and find the right next step.\n\nNeighborhood profiles and map-based orientation\n\nEvents and community activity\n\nMeeting agendas and minutes\n\nCommunity posting guidelines\n\nCNA workshop materials for forming or strengthening a neighborhood association\n\nHow WPCNA works\n\nGovernance, by-laws, and committees\n\nWPCNA’s by-laws and committee work help give the council structure. They support regular communication among neighborhood associations, provide a way to track issues, and help organize discussion around citywide topics.\n\nIf you are looking for governance materials, committee information, or guidance on how the council is organized, contact WPCNA and someone can point you in the right direction."
