      "url": "/events/library-3d-printing-for-teens-2026-07-29/",
      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "Curious about 3D printing?",
      "text": "Curious about 3D printing?\n\nLearning\n\n3D Printing for Teens\n\nCurious about 3D printing?\n\nAbout this event\n\nCurious about 3D printing? Join us for a hands-on class that introduces the basics of 3D design using TinkerCAD, a free and beginner-friendly web-based program. Learn how to create simple 3D models and see how designs are brought to life with a 3D printer. No experience needed - just bring your creativity! This series is for teens in grades 7-12 (as of fall 2026). Registration is required; participants must attend all four days of the series. This program is made possible through the generous support of New York-Presbyterian. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nWednesday, July 29, 2026\n\nTime\n\n1:00 PM - 2:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\n3D Printing for Teens\n\nJul 30, 2026\n\nCurious about 3D printing?\n\nCooking Up Community\n\nJul 22, 2026\n\nJoin Chef Giovanni Green of Break Bread not Hearts for four days of healthy AND delicious cooking!\n\nCooking Up Community\n\nJul 23, 2026\n\nJoin Chef Giovanni Green of Break Bread not Hearts for four days of healthy AND delicious cooking!"
