      "excerpt": "The evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.",
      "text": "The evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.\n\nLearning\n\nComité Noviembre: Reception\n\nThe evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.\n\nAbout this event\n\nThe evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments. The event is free but registration is required. Comit&eacute; Noviembre is a NY-based organization committed to preserving, honoring, and celebrating the deep cultural roots and lived experiences of the Puerto Rican diaspora in New York, across the U.S., and on the island. The exhibit will be on view in the Library's Museum Gallery through September 1. &iexcl;Que Viva Puerto Rico! Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nThursday, July 16, 2026\n\nTime\n\n7:00 PM - 8:45 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nMusical BINGO: A Self-Care Sound Session\n\nJul 26, 2026\n\nJoin us for the ultimate stress relief at our 90s & 2000s Musical Bingo event!\n\nWhite Plains in 1776 (History via Igloo)\n\nJul 29, 2026\n\nLearn about events in White Plains during the crucial year of 1776."
