      "excerpt": "Introduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with…",
      "text": "Introduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with…\n\nLearning\n\nComputer Basics\n\nIntroduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with…\n\nAbout this event\n\nIntroduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with technology. Participants will learn how to use a mouse and keyboard, navigate a computer, and understand basic terminology. The class will also cover how to browse the internet, set up and use email, and practice essential skills for everyday use. No prior experience is needed. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nMonday, September 21, 2026\n\nTime\n\n1:00 PM - 3:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nSep 17, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nRev250 Book Talk: George Washington's War in the North\n\nSep 19, 2026\n\nDenham's book examines Washington's northern campaigns after the Battle of Monmouth in 1778.\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict."
