      "text": "Children in grades 2-5 with their families will create an altar honoring a very special person already departed.\n\nWorkshop\n\nDay of the Dead Altar-Making Workshop\n\nChildren in grades 2-5 with their families will create an altar honoring a very special person already departed.\n\nAbout this event\n\nChildren in grades 2-5 with their families will create an altar honoring a very special person already departed. Families will sign-up for the entire series to allow time to create the altars. On the final day of the series we will have a celebration honoring the departed loved-ones, and the altars will remain on display for the month of November in the Trove. Registration begins on October 1st at the Trove info desk, the Compass. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nFriday, October 9, 2026\n\nTime\n\n4:30 PM - 5:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nIn-Person Registration: Day of the Dead Altar Workshop\n\nOct 1, 2026\n\nChildren in grades 2-5 with their families will create an altar honoring a very special person already departed.\n\nDay of the Dead Altar-Making Workshop\n\nOct 16, 2026\n\nChildren in grades 2-5 with their families will create an altar honoring a very special person already departed.\n\nDay of the Dead Altar-Making Workshop\n\nOct 23, 2026\n\nChildren in grades 2-5 with their families will create an altar honoring a very special person already departed."
