      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "This comprehensive program is designed for people who already have Medicare, as well as those soon to be 65, planning their retirement, or assisting relatives…",
      "text": "This comprehensive program is designed for people who already have Medicare, as well as those soon to be 65, planning their retirement, or assisting relatives…\n\nCivic\n\nDemystifying Medicare\n\nThis comprehensive program is designed for people who already have Medicare, as well as those soon to be 65, planning their retirement, or assisting relatives…\n\nAbout this event\n\nThis comprehensive program is designed for people who already have Medicare, as well as those soon to be 65, planning their retirement, or assisting relatives and friends with paperwork and medical decisions. Topics include Medicare Parts A, B and D, Medigaps, Medicare Advantage and cost-saving programs - a lot to cover, but we try to keep it all upbeat and entertaining. REGISTRATION RECOMMENDED at (914) 231-3236. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nSunday, October 25, 2026\n\nTime\n\n1:15 PM - 4:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nStretch you dough\n\nOct 6, 2026\n\nLearn practical strategies for preparing nutritious, delicious meals without overspending.\n\nDestination College Workshop Series\n\nAug 10, 2026\n\nWorkshop 11: Pathways Beyond College (Trade Schools, Gap Years & Entrepreneurship) Focus: Exploring nontraditional and hands-on paths to success.\n\nJazz at Noon: Vanisha Gould\n\nSep 25, 2026\n\nA Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York's jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally."
