      "text": "Workshop 12: The Transition Ahead (Decisions, Deposits &amp; Life Skills) Focus: Preparing for independence and success after high school.\n\nWorkshop\n\nDestination College Workshop Series\n\nWorkshop 12: The Transition Ahead (Decisions, Deposits & Life Skills) Focus: Preparing for independence and success after high school.\n\nAbout this event\n\nWorkshop 12: The Transition Ahead (Decisions, Deposits & Life Skills) Focus: Preparing for independence and success after high school. &bull; Comparing admission and financial aid offers &bull; Making final decisions and completing deposits &bull; Essential life skills: budgeting, time management, and self-advocacy Takeaway Tool: College Transition Checklist + Reflection Journal Facilitator: Anjanie Narine, Author of Destination College: A Four-Year Plan for High School Students (Second Edition) Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nMonday, August 24, 2026\n\nTime\n\n7:00 PM - 8:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nPowerful Public Speaking & Presentation Skills\n\nJul 28, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester.\n\nWOW Factor: Developing Your Personal Brand\n\nAug 5, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester What is YOUR personal brand saying about you?\n\nResume Writing in the 21st Century\n\nAug 19, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester."
