      "excerpt": "Youth participants of all levels will be able to engage with engineering through hands-on challenges and creative problem-solving.",
      "text": "Youth participants of all levels will be able to engage with engineering through hands-on challenges and creative problem-solving.\n\nLearning\n\nEngineering Camp for Youth\n\nYouth participants of all levels will be able to engage with engineering through hands-on challenges and creative problem-solving.\n\nAbout this event\n\nYouth participants of all levels will be able to engage with engineering through hands-on challenges and creative problem-solving. Led by Digital Media Specialist Austin Olney. Registration is for all four days. Please register only if you can attend all four days. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nFriday, August 7, 2026\n\nTime\n\n12:00 PM - 1:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nArtificial Intelligence (A.I.) in the Igloo\n\nJul 8, 2026\n\nLearn about the current state of Artificial Intelligence (A.I.) and some of the exciting possibilities.\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nWhite Plains in 1776 (History via Igloo)\n\nJul 29, 2026\n\nLearn about events in White Plains during the crucial year of 1776."
