      "id": "page:/events/library-finding-the-best-college-fit-2026-09-21/",
      "sourceId": "page:/events/library-finding-the-best-college-fit-2026-09-21/",
      "title": "Finding the Best College Fit",
      "url": "/events/library-finding-the-best-college-fit-2026-09-21/",
      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "There are over 2,000 four-year colleges in the United States for students to consider.",
      "text": "There are over 2,000 four-year colleges in the United States for students to consider.\n\nWorkshop\n\nFinding the Best College Fit\n\nThere are over 2,000 four-year colleges in the United States for students to consider.\n\nAbout this event\n\nThere are over 2,000 four-year colleges in the United States for students to consider. Needless to say, finding your perfect fit can be overwhelming. Am idst the sea of lists, rankings, and opinions - it can feel like you'll be researching forever. But don't fret, we're here to help! Join us online on 11/30 @ 6:30pm as Jordan Kanarek, Partner at Collegewise and Founder of Kanarek Consulting, shares ways to. -Evaluate the many factors that need to be considered when picking a college -Determine the tools and strategies to research your best-fit college choices -Learn how to plan a college visit to make the most out of your trip -Discuss how best to approach this for your family and financial needs! Come and let us help you navigate the maze of college choices and empower you with with the tools to find the right fit for you. Spots are limited, register today! The program will be presented in partnership with: John C. Hart Memorial Library, New Rochelle Public Library, Port Chester-Rye Brook Public Library, & Warner Library. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nMonday, September 21, 2026\n\nTime\n\n6:30 PM - 7:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nPowerful Public Speaking & Presentation Skills\n\nSep 15, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester.\n\nClean Energy Workforce Opportuntiy\n\nOct 6, 2026\n\nSustainable Westchester, in partnership with Healthy Home Academy, is offering a FREE 5-week Clean Energy Workforce Training program.\n\nVirtual Clean Energy Workforce Opportuntiy\n\nOct 14, 2026\n\nSustainable Westchester, in partnership with Healthy Home Academy, is offering a FREE 5-week Clean Energy Workforce Training program."
