      "excerpt": "The premise of this highly praised work, set in 1930-31 Paris and London, and based on a true event, is that five famous female mystery writers, including…",
      "text": "The premise of this highly praised work, set in 1930-31 Paris and London, and based on a true event, is that five famous female mystery writers, including…\n\nLearning\n\nFuture is Female\n\nThe premise of this highly praised work, set in 1930-31 Paris and London, and based on a true event, is that five famous female mystery writers, including…\n\nAbout this event\n\nThe premise of this highly praised work, set in 1930-31 Paris and London, and based on a true event, is that five famous female mystery writers, including Dorothy Sayers and Agatha Christie, form a secret society to solve a real murder, in order to prove they are equal to men in a male-dominated literary world. This book is available through our catalog in the Library's physical collection and as both an ebook and audiobook in Libby. To join, Click This Zoom Link. You can also use the following phone number to call in: +1 929 436 2866 US (New York). Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nMonday, September 14, 2026\n\nTime\n\n2:00 PM - 3:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nSep 17, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nRev250 Book Talk: George Washington's War in the North\n\nSep 19, 2026\n\nDenham's book examines Washington's northern campaigns after the Battle of Monmouth in 1778.\n\nComputer Basics\n\nSep 21, 2026\n\nIntroduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with…"
