      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "Born in Missouri to enslaved parents just two weeks before the Civil War ended, Carver was one of the most prominent black scientists of the 20th century.",
      "text": "Born in Missouri to enslaved parents just two weeks before the Civil War ended, Carver was one of the most prominent black scientists of the 20th century.\n\nLearning\n\nGeorge Washington Carver: Genius Behind The Peanut Man\n\nBorn in Missouri to enslaved parents just two weeks before the Civil War ended, Carver was one of the most prominent black scientists of the 20th century.\n\nAbout this event\n\nBorn in Missouri to enslaved parents just two weeks before the Civil War ended, Carver was one of the most prominent black scientists of the 20th century. He developed farming techniques to prevent soil depletion, encouraged poor farmers to grow peanuts and sweet potatoes to improve their quality of life, and was an early promoter of environmentalism. Registration for this Zoom program is required. Sign up here! This presentation is offered in collaboration with the Town of Pelham Public Library and other Westchester Libraries. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nThursday, August 6, 2026\n\nTime\n\n11:00 AM - 12:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nSpies in Disguise: Zoom Virtual Program\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nFrom the birth of our nation, women have served alongside men, helping to create the United States of Am erica during the Am erican Revolution.\n\nTech Skills for Success REGISTRATION\n\nJul 6, 2026\n\nDATES: JULY 13, 14, 15, 16, 17 TIME: 2:00PM - 5:00PM IN-PERSON REGISTRATION: JULY 6 FROM 2PM - 5PM This program is limited to 15 people and is on a first…"
