      "text": "International Overdose Awareness Day is observed in more than 40 countries as a time to raise awareness about overdose, reduce stigma, and remember lives that…\n\nLearning\n\nInternational Overdose Awareness Day Event\n\nInternational Overdose Awareness Day is observed in more than 40 countries as a time to raise awareness about overdose, reduce stigma, and remember lives that…\n\nAbout this event\n\nInternational Overdose Awareness Day is observed in more than 40 countries as a time to raise awareness about overdose, reduce stigma, and remember lives that have been lost. By raising awareness, mental health professionals hope to communicate that overdose can be prevented, and that harm and death do not have to be the outcome of overdose. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nMonday, August 31, 2026\n\nTime\n\n5:00 PM - 7:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nComité Noviembre: Reception\n\nJul 16, 2026\n\nThe evening will feature an intimate discussion with Chairwoman Teresa Santiago, accompanied by featured artists, music, light bites, and refreshments.\n\nR&B Soul Line Dancing\n\nAug 8, 2026\n\nDance your way to better balance, coordination, and focus - all while having a great time!\n\nFree Summer Meals at the Library\n\nAug 12, 2026\n\nYouth up to age 18 can get a free lunch at the Library from 11:30-1."
