      "excerpt": "A Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York&#39;s jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally.",
      "text": "A Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York&#39;s jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally.\n\nCivic\n\nJazz at Noon: Vanisha Gould\n\nA Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York's jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally.\n\nAbout this event\n\nA Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York's jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally. Her acclaimed albums In Her Words (2021), Life's a Gig (2024) and She's Not Shiny, She's Not Smooth (2024) center women's experiences with wit and honesty. In 2023, she received The Jazz Gallery Composition Residency Commission, advancing her work in large-scale, interdisciplinary performance. Visit Website Watch on You Tube Check out the full Jazz Fest White Plains lineup here! Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nFriday, September 25, 2026\n\nTime\n\n12:00 PM - 1:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nWhite Plains Sustainability Committee\n\nOct 3, 2026\n\nBring in your broken household items and work with a volunteer Repair Coach to fix them!\n\nWhite Plains Sustainability Committee\n\nNov 21, 2026\n\nBring in your broken household items and work with a volunteer Repair Coach to fix them!\n\nColor Him Father\n\nSep 23, 2026\n\nSeptember is \"Color Him Father\" Month The New York Fathering Conference Committee, the White Plains Youth Bureau, Grandpas United, and Jump Start for Dads are…"
