      "id": "page:/events/library-resume-writing-in-the-21st-century-2026-08-19/",
      "sourceId": "page:/events/library-resume-writing-in-the-21st-century-2026-08-19/",
      "title": "Resume Writing in the 21st Century",
      "url": "/events/library-resume-writing-in-the-21st-century-2026-08-19/",
      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "We will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester.",
      "text": "We will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester.\n\nWorkshop\n\nResume Writing in the 21st Century\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester.\n\nAbout this event\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester. Today's hiring process has evolved way beyond emailing resumes to human resources offices. Participants will learn to break down the sections of the resume and find out how to develop their very own! In addition, applicant tracking systems (ATS) information is shared, how companies use them to help streamline their recruitment processes and what that means when writing a resume. And so much more! Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nWednesday, August 19, 2026\n\nTime\n\n6:00 PM - 7:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nPowerful Public Speaking & Presentation Skills\n\nJul 28, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester.\n\nWOW Factor: Developing Your Personal Brand\n\nAug 5, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester What is YOUR personal brand saying about you?\n\nDestination College Workshop Series\n\nAug 24, 2026\n\nWorkshop 12: The Transition Ahead (Decisions, Deposits & Life Skills) Focus: Preparing for independence and success after high school."
