      "excerpt": "Denham&#39;s book examines Washington&#39;s northern campaigns after the Battle of Monmouth in 1778.",
      "text": "Denham&#39;s book examines Washington&#39;s northern campaigns after the Battle of Monmouth in 1778.\n\nLearning\n\nRev250 Book Talk: George Washington's War in the North\n\nDenham's book examines Washington's northern campaigns after the Battle of Monmouth in 1778.\n\nAbout this event\n\nDenham's book examines Washington's northern campaigns after the Battle of Monmouth in 1778. These campaigns are often overlooked but they show Washington's great skill in strategy, logistics, and diplomacy. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nSaturday, September 19, 2026\n\nTime\n\n2:00 PM - 3:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nSep 17, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nWestchester During the Revolutionary War (History via Igloo)\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nLearn about Westchester County during the Revolutionary War and what happened throughout the conflict.\n\nComputer Basics\n\nSep 21, 2026\n\nIntroduction to Computers: Learn the Basics This beginner-friendly class is designed for those who are new to computers or looking to build confidence with…"
