      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "Learn practical strategies for preparing nutritious, delicious meals without overspending.",
      "text": "Learn practical strategies for preparing nutritious, delicious meals without overspending.\n\nCivic\n\nStretch you dough\n\nLearn practical strategies for preparing nutritious, delicious meals without overspending.\n\nAbout this event\n\nLearn practical strategies for preparing nutritious, delicious meals without overspending. In this interactive workshop, participants will discover budget-friendly meal planning tips, smart grocery shopping techniques, and creative ways to make ingredients go further. Presented by Feeding Westchester, this program will help you maximize your food budget while creating healthy and satisfying meals for yourself and your family. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nTuesday, October 6, 2026\n\nTime\n\n1:00 PM - 2:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nDemystifying Medicare\n\nOct 25, 2026\n\nThis comprehensive program is designed for people who already have Medicare, as well as those soon to be 65, planning their retirement, or assisting relatives…\n\nDestination College Workshop Series\n\nAug 10, 2026\n\nWorkshop 11: Pathways Beyond College (Trade Schools, Gap Years & Entrepreneurship) Focus: Exploring nontraditional and hands-on paths to success.\n\nJazz at Noon: Vanisha Gould\n\nSep 25, 2026\n\nA Berklee College of Music graduate, Vanisha Gould is a key voice in New York's jazz scene, performing at leading venues and touring internationally."
