      "url": "/events/library-unclaimed-funds-workshop-2026-10-29/",
      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "Does New York State have money in your name?",
      "text": "Does New York State have money in your name?\n\nWorkshop\n\nUnclaimed Funds Workshop\n\nDoes New York State have money in your name?\n\nAbout this event\n\nDoes New York State have money in your name? The State has billions of dollars in lost money. Each day they return about a million dollars to those who file claims. In this workshop you will find out what kind of funds are held, how to file a claim and estate items. No appointment or registration are needed. Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nUpcoming\n\nDate\n\nThursday, October 29, 2026\n\nTime\n\n4:00 PM - 6:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nPowerful Public Speaking & Presentation Skills\n\nSep 15, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester.\n\nFinding the Best College Fit\n\nSep 21, 2026\n\nThere are over 2,000 four-year colleges in the United States for students to consider.\n\nClean Energy Workforce Opportuntiy\n\nOct 6, 2026\n\nSustainable Westchester, in partnership with Healthy Home Academy, is offering a FREE 5-week Clean Energy Workforce Training program."
