      "type": "event",
      "excerpt": "Join us for Unearth a Story, a generative writing workshop designed to help participants uncover the stories inside you!",
      "text": "Join us for Unearth a Story, a generative writing workshop designed to help participants uncover the stories inside you!\n\nWorkshop\n\nUnearth a Story\n\nJoin us for Unearth a Story, a generative writing workshop designed to help participants uncover the stories inside you!\n\nAbout this event\n\nJoin us for Unearth a Story, a generative writing workshop designed to help participants uncover the stories inside you! This generative writing workshop guides participants through prompts and exercises to spark creativity and produce new pieces of writing. Through reflection, and creative exploration, writers of all levels will discover new ideas, tap into personal experiences, and develop their unique voice in a welcoming and supportive environment. Ideal for ages 14+ and all experience levels. No writing experience is necessary-just bring your curiosity and imagination! Check the library page for registration, tickets, and any schedule updates.\n\nAt a Glance\n\nStatus\n\nPast\n\nDate\n\nTuesday, July 14, 2026\n\nTime\n\n6:00 PM - 7:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nAddress\n\n100 Martine Avenue, White Plains, NY 10601\n\nSource\n\nWhite Plains Public Library\n\nMore Events\n\nRelated events\n\nIntroduction to Drawing\n\nJul 15, 2026\n\nLearn to draw step by step Program will be hosted by Lila from The Kraft Dealer.\n\nIntroduction to Drawing\n\nJul 18, 2026\n\nLearn to draw step by step Program will be hosted by Lila from The Kraft Dealer.\n\nPowerful Public Speaking & Presentation Skills\n\nJul 28, 2026\n\nWe will be hosting the following program in partnership with The College of Westchester."
